+## Overview
+
+Date pickers allow users to select a single or a range of dates. Pickers are
+used to display past, present, or future dates. The kind of date (exact,
+approximate, memorable) you are requesting from the user will determine which
+picker is best to use. Each picker's format can be customized depending on
+location or need. The `cds-preview-date-picker` component expects one or more
+`cds-preview-date-picker-input` elements as children.
+
+<Canvas of={DatePickerStories.SingleWithCalendar} />
+
+### Simple date picker
+
+The simple date input provides the user with only a text field in which they can
+manually input a date. It allows dates to be entered without adding unnecessary
+interactions that come with the calendar menu or a dropdown.
+
+<Canvas of={DatePickerStories.Simple} />
+
+### Single date picker
+
+Use the single date picker when you want to pair a text input with a calendar
+popover. Users can type a date directly, or open the calendar and select one.
+
+<Canvas of={DatePickerStories.SingleWithCalendar} />
+
+### Range date picker
+
+Use the range date picker when users need to choose a start and end date
+together. The first input should use `kind="from"` and the second should use
+`kind="to"`.
+
+<Canvas of={DatePickerStories.RangeWithCalendar} />
+
+### Skeleton state
+
+You can use the `cds-preview-date-picker-input-skeleton` component to render a
+skeleton variant of a date picker. This is useful while the initial state or
+date range is loading.
+
+<Canvas of={DatePickerStories.Skeleton} />
+
+### AI label
+
+The input supports Carbon AI label content as slotted child content.
+
+<Canvas of={DatePickerStories.WithAILabel} />
+
+## Component API
+
+### API Compatibility
+
+This implementation keeps the attribute/property surface close to the existing
+Carbon Web Components date picker API while replacing the internal
+Flatpickr-based behavior with shared primitives and a state machine.
+
+**`cds-preview-date-picker` attributes/properties:**
+
+- `date-format` - Date display format (default: `m/d/Y`)
+- `disabled` - Disable the date picker
+- `max-date` - Maximum selectable date
+- `min-date` - Minimum selectable date
+- `name` - Form field name for form submission
+- `readonly` - Make the date picker read-only
+- `value` - Selected date value
+
+**`cds-preview-date-picker-input` attributes/properties:**
+
+- `color-scheme` - Color scheme variant
+- `disabled` - Disable the input
+- `hide-label` - Hide the label text
+- `invalid` - Show invalid state
+- `invalid-text` - Invalid state message
+- `kind` - Input type (`simple`, `single`, `from`, `to`)
+- `label-text` - Label text
+- `pattern` - Input validation pattern
+- `placeholder` - Placeholder text
+- `readonly` - Make input read-only
+- `required` - Mark as required field
+- `short` - Use short variant
+- `size` - Input size (`sm`, `md`, `lg`)
+- `type` - Input type
+- `value` - Input value
+- `warn` - Show warning state
+- `warn-text` - Warning state message
+
+**Events:**
+
+- `cds-preview-date-picker-changed` - Fired when date selection changes
+- `cds-preview-date-picker-error` - Fired when an error occurs
+
+### Breaking Changes
+
+**Tag renames.** All elements use new `cds-preview-*` tag names:
+
+| Classic v11               | Preview                           |
+| ------------------------- | --------------------------------- |
+| `<cds-date-picker>`       | `<cds-preview-date-picker>`       |
+| `<cds-date-picker-input>` | `<cds-preview-date-picker-input>` |
+
+**Import path.** The preview registers from a different module path:
+
+```diff
+- import '@carbon/web-components/es/components/date-picker/index.js';
++ import '@carbon/web-components/es/components/date-picker/next/index.js';
+```
+
+**Change event name and `detail` shape.** Update all listeners:
+
+```diff
+- el.addEventListener('cds-date-picker-changed', (e) => { /* flatpickr detail */ });
++ el.addEventListener('cds-preview-date-picker-changed', (e) => {
++   const { selectedDates, value } = e.detail;
++   // selectedDates: Temporal.PlainDate[]
++   // value: ISO string, range dates joined with "/"
++ });
+```
+
+**No Flatpickr APIs.** The preview is not backed by Flatpickr. Its format
+tokens, options, and instance API are unavailable. `date-format` accepts basic
+numeric tokens only: `m`, `d`, `Y`.
+
+**What changed internally:**
+
+- Removed Flatpickr dependency (~15,000 lines of code)
+- Implemented native calendar using Temporal API, Popover API, and CSS Anchor
+  Positioning
+- Added state machine for predictable behavior
+- Enhanced keyboard navigation
+- Improved accessibility
